cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this material, please cite it as below."
title: "Gjenopptak: obstacle types behind authors' own statements of undone work"
abstract: >-
  A preregistered study of how often researchers record work they did not get
  done, and which obstacles they name. Four purposively chosen fields, 100
  open-access works, 22,243 passages judged by a local model and a stratified
  sample read blind against a typology locked before data collection. A
  prospective phase on 100 further archaeology works (ADDENDUM-25) passed a
  blind precision gate fixed before the draw and gave the first measured
  recall of the sieve.
type: software
